diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index de1a214..9c44f74 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -12,6 +12,12 @@
 - Fix `item()` and `dumps()` writing a `datetime` whose UTC offset is not a whole number of minutes (e.g. the historical LMT offsets `zoneinfo` gives, such as `-00:44:30`) as invalid TOML like `1900-01-01T12:00:00Z:30`, which no parser accepts. Such a value is now written as the same instant in UTC; this also covers `DateTime.replace()` and `astimezone()`.
 - Allow `DateTime.astimezone()` to use the local timezone when no timezone argument is supplied, matching `datetime.datetime`.
 - Arithmetic and `replace()` results for `Integer`, `Float`, `String`, `DateTime`, `Date` and `Time` no longer share the original item's `Trivia`, so changing the result's comment or indentation no longer rewrites the item still stored in the document.
+- Fix tables defined in several non-contiguous parts of a document:
+  - a table split by an array of tables (e.g. `[tool.poetry]`, `[[plugins]]`, `[tool.other]`) no longer has its parts merged and reordered on `as_string()`;
+  - the parser now applies the same table/key definition rules as `tomllib`, so valid documents are no longer rejected (or fail when accessed) and invalid ones (e.g. a table declared again after being defined with dotted keys) are no longer accepted;
+  - a sub-table of an array of tables element written after other tables (`[[a]]` ... `[x]` ... `[a.y]`) stays in place, and the array is presented as one list;
+  - setting, replacing, deleting, `pop()` and `update()` on a split table (including nested ones) only touch the affected key in the affected parts instead of dropping whole parts, and put new keys in a part where they produce valid TOML;
+  - tables added under a dotted key (`a.b = 1`) are written with a header after the enclosing table's keys instead of in the middle of it, and dotted-key tables no longer turn into misplaced headers when they gain a value.
 
 ## [0.15.2] - 2026-10-16
 
